$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure D: In a screw cap tube,
bromopyrazole (1 equiv.), phenylboronic acid (1.2 equiv.), Pd(dtbpf)Cl2
(0.1 equiv.) and K2CO3 (1.5 equiv.), were added in acetonitrile/water
(1/1, 0.1 M). The reaction mixture was stirred at 100 °C overnight, then
filtered on celite and washed with ethyl acetate. The filtrate was then
washed with brine. The organic layer were collected, dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate and evaporated under vacuum. The crude mixture was
purified by column chromatography. •
1-(4-methylphenyl)-5-phenyl-4-(2-phenylethyl)-1H-pyrazole (6a) Entry: 5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper(I)-Catalyzed Cycloaddition of 4-Bromosydnones and Alkynes for the
Regioselective Synthesis of 1,4,5-Trisubstituted Pyrazoles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
